      "description": "Watch Cruzeiro vs Botafogo highlights and goals from Brasileirão on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 26, 2026. On July 26, 2026, the stage was set for a high-stakes Serie A encounter in Brazil as Cruzeiro faced off against Botafogo in a match defined by tactical discipline and late-game drama. Clinical Finish Breaks the Deadlock The opening period was a physical affair, with the referee forced to reach for his pocket early on to caution Warleson and Huguinho . Amidst the grind, a moment of pure quality separated the two sides in the 41st minute. Alex Telles turned provider with a perfectly weighted assist, finding Gabriel Justino , who made no mistake in slotting the ball home. This goal provided Botafogo with a vital lead heading into the break, shifting the momentum of the contest. Tactical Shifts in the Second Half As the second half got underway, both managers looked to their benches to influence the flow of the game. Cruzeiro introduced the likes of Kauan Toledo and Keny Arroyo to inject pace into their attack, while Botafogo responded by bringing on defensive reinforcements such as Lucas Villalba and Fernando Marcal . The match remained balanced but increasingly fractious, with Jonathan Jesus picking up a yellow card as the home side struggled to break down a resilient defensive line. A Frantic and Heated Conclusion The final stages of the match saw tensions boil over as both teams fought desperately for the next goal. The referee had a busy conclusion to the evening, issuing a flurry of yellow cards in stoppage time to Alex Telles , Kadir Barria , Keny Arroyo , and Kaio Jorge . Despite the late pressure and the rising emotions on the pitch, the visitors held firm to secure a hard-fought victory, leaving the home fans disappointed in a match that was contested until the very last whistle."
